WEBVTT

00:25.910 --> 00:29.870
<b>The Foundation Festival
is really starting!</b>

02:00.000 --> 02:05.010
<b>"Episode 12"
"Ryoma and the Town of Gimul"</b>

02:09.260 --> 02:13.100
<b>Mr. Asagi, Miss Miya, good morning!</b>

02:13.100 --> 02:15.060
<b>Oh, Ryoma.</b>

02:15.060 --> 02:16.770
<b>Morning!</b>

02:16.770 --> 02:18.350
<b>How is it?</b>

02:18.350 --> 02:19.980
<b>We're ready.</b>

02:19.980 --> 02:23.900
<b>Now we can offer this to many people
for their enjoyment.</b>

02:23.900 --> 02:26.530
<b>Okay, I'll stop by again later.</b>

02:26.530 --> 02:27.900
<b>We'll be waiting.</b>

02:27.900 --> 02:30.370
<b>Good luck to you, too, Ryoma.</b>

02:30.370 --> 02:31.950
<b>Thanks.</b>

02:44.460 --> 02:46.720
<b>Oh, this tune...</b>

02:54.010 --> 02:58.770
<b>The tune you just heard is the piece
we the Semroid Troupe</b>

02:58.770 --> 03:02.440
<b>will be performing on stage tonight.</b>

03:02.440 --> 03:07.780
<b>The very same tune can be played
on this "music box" magic item...</b>

03:09.320 --> 03:13.120
<b>Any time you please.</b>

03:14.620 --> 03:17.290
<b>Mr. Serge, good morning.</b>

03:17.290 --> 03:22.250
<b>Mr. Ryoma. The music box
seems to be gaining popularity.</b>

03:22.250 --> 03:26.840
<b>I have to thank the Semroid Troupe
for their advertisement.</b>

03:26.840 --> 03:31.010
<b>Dinome's Workshop at Keleban is
hard at work mass-producing them.</b>

03:31.010 --> 03:35.180
<b>We plan to widen the sales network soon.</b>

03:38.730 --> 03:43.940
<b>It should serve that family well,
as fond memorabilia of today.</b>

03:43.940 --> 03:45.190
<b>Yes.</b>

03:47.480 --> 03:51.360
<b>I'm really happy.</b>

03:51.360 --> 03:53.070
<b>Such a crowd already?!</b>

03:53.070 --> 03:55.700
<b>--Next customer!
--Vegetable stir-fry, ready!</b>

03:55.700 --> 03:57.200
<b>--One semesa pastry,
and that grain tea thing, please.</b>

03:57.200 --> 03:58.950
<b>--Thank you!
--One semesa pastry,
and that grain tea thing, please.</b>

03:58.950 --> 04:01.790
<b>--Understood.
--Next customer!</b>

04:03.000 --> 04:05.040
<b>Here you are, Mr. Callum.</b>

04:05.040 --> 04:08.880
<b>Thank you. Your order's ready!</b>

04:10.130 --> 04:11.680
<b>Mr. Dolce!</b>

04:13.590 --> 04:14.850
<b>What's wrong?</b>

04:16.640 --> 04:19.810
<b>Can you help with managing the lines?</b>

04:19.810 --> 04:22.940
<b>Understood. Business is good, I suppose?</b>

04:22.940 --> 04:25.190
<b>--Wow, delicious!
--Yes, the foreign delicacies
are being received well, too.</b>

04:25.190 --> 04:26.730
<b>--Yes, the foreign delicacies
are being received well, too.</b>

04:26.730 --> 04:30.030
<b>That's good. Leave this to me.</b>

04:30.030 --> 04:31.450
<b>Yes, please.</b>

04:31.450 --> 04:36.910
<b>Manager! Please go ask Miss Selma
for more stir-fry!</b>

04:36.910 --> 04:40.540
<b>Also, we're running out of grain tea!</b>

04:40.540 --> 04:42.120
<b>Understood!</b>

04:47.790 --> 04:49.880
<b>I'm counting on you.</b>

04:49.880 --> 04:51.130
<b>Out of my way!</b>

04:51.130 --> 04:52.630
<b>Oops, sorry.</b>

04:52.630 --> 04:55.800
<b>Wow, we're busy!</b>

04:58.100 --> 05:02.310
<b>Miss Selma, more stir-fry please!</b>

05:02.310 --> 05:06.020
<b>I thought it would run out around now,
so I'm already working on it.</b>

05:06.020 --> 05:07.770
<b>Thank you!</b>

05:07.770 --> 05:12.780
<b>Oh, also, Miss Fina,
could you make more grain tea, as well?</b>

05:12.780 --> 05:14.910
<b>Understood!</b>

05:14.910 --> 05:18.030
<b>Manager, this is awesome!</b>

05:18.030 --> 05:20.660
<b>The vegetables, so quickly...!</b>

05:20.660 --> 05:25.710
<b>The cooking tool based on
transformed slime. I'm glad it's helping!</b>

05:25.710 --> 05:27.130
<b>Now...</b>

05:28.670 --> 05:30.340
<b>Everyone!</b>

05:32.130 --> 05:34.300
<b>Take care of this, too!</b>

05:40.470 --> 05:43.600
<b>You look busy, Ryoma.</b>

05:43.600 --> 05:45.270
<b>Mr. Worgan!</b>

05:45.270 --> 05:48.100
<b>You all seem to be working hard, too.</b>

05:48.100 --> 05:54.070
<b>Of course! We got hired,
so we'll do our best!</b>

05:54.070 --> 05:56.240
<b>They're really helping out a lot.</b>

05:56.240 --> 05:59.200
<b>They've been here
since the early preparations...</b>

06:01.080 --> 06:03.950
<b>Wait, they've been working non-stop...</b>

06:03.950 --> 06:07.960
<b>They haven't had a chance
to enjoy the festival!</b>

06:07.960 --> 06:12.500
<b>Mr. Worgan, can you take Beck and
the other kids out to see the festival?</b>

06:12.500 --> 06:14.460
<b>Sure, I guess.</b>

06:14.460 --> 06:20.260
<b>What are you talking about?! We're so busy,
we can't just take off and go play!</b>

06:20.260 --> 06:23.220
<b>We can take care of the work.</b>

06:23.220 --> 06:26.180
<b>Miss Carla! And Mr. Caulkin and everyone!</b>

06:26.180 --> 06:30.270
<b>I heard from Callum. We're here to help.</b>

06:32.860 --> 06:34.650
<b>--Yum.
--Nice!</b>

06:35.650 --> 06:41.120
<b>The second shop in Lenaf
is being handled by the new hires.</b>

06:41.120 --> 06:45.160
<b>They're already well accustomed to the job,
so there's nothing to worry about.</b>

06:45.160 --> 06:48.870
<b>I see. I'm glad you came to help.</b>

06:48.870 --> 06:53.040
<b>Now we can get everyone
to take turns taking breaks.</b>

06:58.260 --> 07:01.340
<b>Yes, which means
you should rest, too, Manager.</b>

07:01.340 --> 07:03.310
<b>What? But I...</b>

07:03.310 --> 07:08.770
<b>This is your first Foundation Festival,
as well. Please go enjoy it.</b>

07:08.770 --> 07:14.980
<b>Oh, thank you. But there are just
a few more things to take care of...</b>

07:23.330 --> 07:25.950
<b>How wonderful!</b>

07:25.950 --> 07:29.370
<b>Mr. Prenance! Are you all right?</b>

07:29.370 --> 07:33.380
<b>This place is very cold because of
the barrier and the ice magic.</b>

07:33.380 --> 07:39.470
<b>The beauty of this wonderful statue
makes the cold completely unnoticeable!</b>

07:39.470 --> 07:41.430
<b>Huh?</b>

07:41.430 --> 07:44.510
<b>Oh, words cannot express my gratitude.</b>

07:45.310 --> 07:49.930
<b>I must perform my very best to match
the magnificence of this statue.</b>

07:49.930 --> 07:53.810
<b>Oh, yes, I'm looking forward to it.</b>

07:56.520 --> 07:59.530
<b>Manager, you've finished.</b>

07:59.530 --> 08:01.030
<b>Yes.</b>

08:01.030 --> 08:03.110
<b>In that case,
please really take that break--</b>

08:03.110 --> 08:07.080
<b>Mr. Ryoma, hello again.</b>

08:07.080 --> 08:10.790
<b>Mr. Serge, you're with Mr. Pioro.</b>

08:10.790 --> 08:13.580
<b>We'd like to talk to you for a bit,
if that's all right.</b>

08:13.580 --> 08:16.000
<b>Sure thing.</b>

08:21.090 --> 08:24.090
<b>This grain tea is very popular.</b>

08:24.090 --> 08:26.260
<b>It's causing quite a stir.</b>

08:26.260 --> 08:29.770
<b>Yes, thanks to everyone,
it's selling well.</b>

08:33.100 --> 08:39.610
<b>It's nice. It has a fragrance
unlike other teas and herbs.</b>

08:39.610 --> 08:42.780
<b>I'm glad you like it.</b>

08:42.780 --> 08:45.120
<b>Where did you get the grains for this?</b>

08:45.120 --> 08:48.410
<b>It's from the hometown
of some of my employees.</b>

08:48.410 --> 08:51.040
<b>They said they couldn't sell them
and have many left over.</b>

08:52.120 --> 08:53.870
<b>--Ryoma!
--Mr. Ryoma!</b>

08:58.960 --> 09:01.130
<b>The grains from our village?</b>

09:01.130 --> 09:07.010
<b>Yes, they want to turn it into grain tea
and make it into a proper business.</b>

09:07.010 --> 09:08.470
<b>Really?!</b>

09:08.470 --> 09:15.440
<b>Yes. The tea is selling very well,
and with Mr. Serge and Mr. Pioro's help,</b>

09:15.440 --> 09:19.440
<b>it should be more than adequate
for a successful business.</b>

09:19.440 --> 09:22.900
<b>I'm so glad! My people back home
would love to hear that, too.</b>

09:22.900 --> 09:25.320
<b>Thank you, Manager!</b>

09:25.320 --> 09:27.410
<b>I didn't do anything...</b>

09:27.410 --> 09:31.290
<b>Let's discuss the details later.</b>

09:31.290 --> 09:34.790
<b>Yes, thank you!</b>

09:34.790 --> 09:37.130
<b>Once they start making profits,
their village won't need to</b>

09:37.130 --> 09:40.170
<b>send off their young people
to distant towns to find work.</b>

09:40.170 --> 09:42.260
<b>I hope that works out.</b>

09:42.260 --> 09:47.090
<b>Manager! Time to finally take your break!</b>

09:47.090 --> 09:50.470
<b>Oh, yes, understood...</b>

09:50.470 --> 09:55.850
<b>Miss Carla is right.
You must enjoy this festival, as well.</b>

09:55.850 --> 09:57.270
<b>Yes.</b>

09:57.270 --> 10:02.940
<b>I have to practice what I preached
to Beck and the others.</b>

10:02.940 --> 10:05.150
<b>Thanks for waiting!</b>

10:05.150 --> 10:07.280
<b>Wow!</b>

10:07.280 --> 10:09.030
<b>Enjoy!</b>

10:09.030 --> 10:11.950
<b>Tenmusu and miso soup.</b>

10:11.950 --> 10:13.660
<b>Thank you for the food.</b>

10:22.500 --> 10:24.880
<b>Yes! This is great!</b>

10:24.880 --> 10:27.970
<b>I made many more improvements
after the last time you tried it.</b>

10:27.970 --> 10:30.850
<b>It's becoming quite popular.</b>

10:33.100 --> 10:39.060
<b>Yes, it's great. I'll advertise it
to my employees, as well.</b>

10:50.160 --> 10:53.410
<b>Mom!</b>

10:54.540 --> 10:57.120
<b>I knew it! A lost child!</b>

10:57.120 --> 10:59.620
<b>Ready? Say cheese!</b>

10:59.620 --> 11:02.460
<b>I'm so glad Mr. Ryoma is so big!</b>

11:02.460 --> 11:04.210
<b>I can finally see Mr. Ryoma again!</b>

11:04.210 --> 11:05.340
<b>I'll send another letter!</b>

11:05.340 --> 11:07.630
<b>Wait, it's over already?!</b>

11:13.300 --> 11:15.060
<b>Where's your mom?</b>

11:17.850 --> 11:19.640
<b>Where do you live?</b>

11:21.440 --> 11:23.480
<b>He's lost.</b>

11:23.480 --> 11:25.860
<b>I haven't seen him around here.</b>

11:25.860 --> 11:27.150
<b>I see.</b>

11:27.150 --> 11:30.910
<b>He must be a visitor from another town.</b>

11:30.910 --> 11:36.620
<b>Let's take him to the guards.
His mother must be looking for him, too!</b>

11:40.710 --> 11:43.880
<b>He seems to like you, Ryoma.</b>

11:49.380 --> 11:51.630
<b>Let's go find your mom.</b>

11:51.630 --> 11:53.140
<b>Yeah.</b>

11:53.140 --> 11:55.180
<b>Okay, I'll go now.</b>

11:55.180 --> 11:57.600
<b>--Yes.
--Counting on you!</b>

11:58.470 --> 12:02.020
<b>I'm Ryoma Takebayashi. What's your name?</b>

12:02.020 --> 12:03.350
<b>Theo.</b>

12:03.350 --> 12:06.900
<b>Theo, huh? Did you come with your mom?</b>

12:06.900 --> 12:07.940
<b>Yes.</b>

12:07.940 --> 12:10.110
<b>Is this your first festival?</b>

12:10.110 --> 12:11.490
<b>Yes, it is.</b>

12:11.490 --> 12:13.780
<b>It's my first time, too, actually.</b>

12:13.780 --> 12:15.280
<b>Really?</b>

12:15.280 --> 12:18.790
<b>Yes. I was somewhere else before.</b>

12:18.790 --> 12:20.290
<b>Where?</b>

12:21.830 --> 12:24.380
<b>A place very far away...</b>

12:25.380 --> 12:29.840
<b>Far away... Yes, Earth.</b>

12:29.840 --> 12:33.800
<b>In Japan, at an exploitative company.</b>

12:33.800 --> 12:40.270
<b>I died, and by the grace of the gods,
I was transferred here.</b>

12:42.350 --> 12:48.150
<b>I met Elia, the Reinbachs, traveled...</b>

12:50.070 --> 12:51.950
<b>Landed here in Gimul...</b>

12:53.280 --> 12:57.280
<b>Opened up Bamboo Forest...</b>

13:00.370 --> 13:03.210
<b>Now that I think about it,
I've come pretty far.</b>

13:04.080 --> 13:05.000
<b>Hmm?</b>

13:05.000 --> 13:08.340
<b>Oh, it's nothing.</b>

13:08.340 --> 13:10.590
<b>Oh, is he lost?</b>

13:12.260 --> 13:17.800
<b>Ms. Glissela. I'm taking him
to the guards' office.</b>

13:17.800 --> 13:20.350
<b>Good work, then.</b>

13:36.360 --> 13:40.370
<b>You've established yourself
as a citizen of this town.</b>

13:40.370 --> 13:41.830
<b>Really?</b>

13:41.830 --> 13:47.630
<b>How does life here compare
to life in the forest?</b>

13:49.090 --> 13:55.510
<b>I can't say which is better.
The forest had its own perks. But...</b>

13:56.970 --> 14:00.010
<b>From the look on your face,
I guess it's fine.</b>

14:00.010 --> 14:02.680
<b>Yes, I agree.</b>

14:02.680 --> 14:05.480
<b>Life here isn't bad either.</b>

14:05.480 --> 14:07.150
<b>Oh, Theo! I'm so glad!</b>

14:07.150 --> 14:10.150
<b>Mom!</b>

14:10.150 --> 14:12.780
<b>Thank you so very much.</b>

14:12.780 --> 14:16.450
<b>Please don't mention it. Bye, Theo!</b>

14:16.450 --> 14:18.200
<b>Bye-bye!</b>

14:21.330 --> 14:26.960
<b>Yeah, life here isn't bad.</b>

14:30.290 --> 14:34.460
<b>The beast that tormented the people
lies vanquished before me.</b>

14:34.460 --> 14:39.340
<b>From today on, it will live among us
and follow a new path.</b>

14:39.340 --> 14:43.770
<b>Let us rejoice this day, and celebrate!</b>

15:26.060 --> 15:30.020
<b>Manager, what is this dish called?</b>

15:30.020 --> 15:31.520
<b>It's "fried noodles."</b>

15:31.520 --> 15:37.070
<b>There are many ways to flavor it,
but I'm keeping it simple today with salt.</b>

15:37.070 --> 15:41.200
<b>Looks delicious. I'll try cooking it
for lunch one day.</b>

15:41.200 --> 15:43.370
<b>Yes, please do.</b>

15:43.370 --> 15:47.540
<b>That should be enough cooking
for the after-party.</b>

15:49.370 --> 15:50.870
<b>Manager.</b>

15:51.960 --> 15:55.550
<b>The Semroid Troupe isn't here yet.</b>

15:55.550 --> 16:00.550
<b>Maybe they're having trouble
cleaning up their stage? I'll go check.</b>

16:06.100 --> 16:08.560
<b>What are they doing...?</b>

16:11.690 --> 16:14.230
<b>Oh, Ryoma.</b>

16:14.230 --> 16:16.110
<b>Thank you for today.</b>

16:16.110 --> 16:18.230
<b>Can we help you?</b>

16:18.230 --> 16:21.820
<b>The after-party is starting,
so I came to invite you all, but...</b>

16:21.820 --> 16:24.370
<b>What are you doing?</b>

16:24.370 --> 16:25.530
<b>Ah.</b>

16:25.530 --> 16:27.910
<b>Is that a divine statue?</b>

16:27.910 --> 16:32.500
<b>You don't see that often, do you?
That's a statue of Manoailoa.</b>

16:32.500 --> 16:34.880
<b>Manoailoa...</b>

16:35.790 --> 16:38.590
<b>I remember that name
from one of the myths.</b>

16:38.590 --> 16:41.590
<b>I haven't met them yet,
but it's definitely a name of a god,</b>

16:41.590 --> 16:44.550
<b>right up there with Gain and the others.</b>

16:44.550 --> 16:47.050
<b>The god of wind, right?</b>

16:47.050 --> 16:53.810
<b>Indeed. A great god that watches over us,
through the winds that travel this world.</b>

16:53.810 --> 16:58.150
<b>Also a god of travels and arts.</b>

16:58.150 --> 17:02.820
<b>Traveling artists often worship Manoailoa!</b>

17:02.820 --> 17:05.950
<b>We were just dressing up the statue.</b>

17:05.950 --> 17:07.160
<b>Dressing up?</b>

17:07.160 --> 17:14.330
<b>Yes. When we experience something memorable,
we buy a piece of cloth in that town.</b>

17:14.330 --> 17:17.590
<b>It's hard to buy stuff while traveling.</b>

17:17.590 --> 17:21.630
<b>The cloth wrapping the statue is
our expression of thanks to the god</b>

17:21.630 --> 17:23.470
<b>for gifting us with a great meeting.</b>

17:23.470 --> 17:27.390
<b>You can call it a tradition
among us traveling entertainers.</b>

17:27.390 --> 17:30.350
<b>I don't know when it started.</b>

17:30.350 --> 17:34.060
<b>Memories while traveling...</b>

17:38.900 --> 17:43.110
<b>Everyone, are you ready?</b>

17:45.360 --> 17:48.410
<b>Manager, take it away.</b>

17:48.410 --> 17:49.620
<b>Yes.</b>

17:52.410 --> 17:57.040
<b>Everyone, thank you for your hard work
at the Foundation Festival.</b>

17:57.040 --> 17:58.250
<b>Cheers!</b>

17:58.250 --> 18:00.210
<b>Cheers!</b>

18:01.250 --> 18:04.550
<b>--It's delicious!
--Yes.
--Nice.</b>

18:08.970 --> 18:12.520
<b>The festival was super fun!</b>

18:12.520 --> 18:16.270
<b>Everyone was able to buy stuff
from the pay we got for working here.</b>

18:16.270 --> 18:19.560
<b>It's all thanks to you, Ryoma.</b>

18:19.560 --> 18:20.770
<b>You're welcome.</b>

18:20.770 --> 18:23.690
<b>Ryoma, did you get a chance
to enjoy the festival?</b>

18:24.780 --> 18:27.070
<b>Yes. After helping a lost boy
find his mom,</b>

18:27.070 --> 18:29.990
<b>I had a look around.</b>

18:29.990 --> 18:31.450
<b>I'm glad.</b>

18:31.450 --> 18:37.250
<b>Miss Carla, I'm so glad
you came from Lenaf.</b>

18:37.250 --> 18:39.130
<b>You were very helpful.</b>

18:39.130 --> 18:44.090
<b>I also enjoyed my first
Foundation Festival. It felt fresh.</b>

18:45.630 --> 18:49.890
<b>I haven't been gone from
this town for too long yet,</b>

18:49.890 --> 18:53.260
<b>but I did feel somewhat nostalgic.</b>

18:53.260 --> 18:54.810
<b>Ryoma.</b>

18:54.810 --> 18:56.890
<b>Oh, Miss Maiya.</b>

18:56.890 --> 19:00.520
<b>Do you want to perform with us
to wrap up the night?</b>

19:00.520 --> 19:01.900
<b>Huh?</b>

19:01.900 --> 19:03.690
<b>Do it, Ryoma!</b>

19:03.690 --> 19:05.990
<b>Yes, please!</b>

19:05.990 --> 19:07.990
<b>--Yeah! Manager!
--We look forward to it!</b>

19:07.990 --> 19:09.780
<b>Do your best!</b>

19:09.780 --> 19:11.530
<b>Understood.</b>

19:11.530 --> 19:13.830
<b>Good luck, Manager.</b>

19:13.830 --> 19:17.040
<b>Yes, I'll enjoy this.</b>

19:52.990 --> 19:55.240
<b>I think I...</b>

20:07.170 --> 20:11.010
<b>...will never forget this day.</b>

20:15.350 --> 20:17.010
<b>Mr. Serge.</b>

20:17.010 --> 20:21.640
<b>Mr. Ryoma, your sword dancing
and music were both wonderful.</b>

20:21.640 --> 20:27.070
<b>Thank you. Um, I have a request.</b>

20:31.530 --> 20:36.620
<b>The Foundation Festival became
a day I won't forget.</b>

20:36.620 --> 20:38.080
<b>To commemorate this day,</b>

20:38.080 --> 20:44.170
<b>I asked Mr. Serge to create
two special music boxes.</b>

20:48.380 --> 20:51.050
<b>I'm sending one to you.</b>

20:56.140 --> 20:58.390
<b>What a beautiful tune.</b>

20:58.390 --> 21:02.020
<b>I'm so glad I came to Gimul.</b>

21:02.020 --> 21:06.440
<b>I was able to find a place
where I can call home.</b>

21:06.440 --> 21:12.900
<b>I'll continue to do my best
to serve this community.</b>

21:16.530 --> 21:18.530
<b>Mr. Ryoma...</b>

21:18.530 --> 21:24.290
<b>I'll also do my best and improve myself.</b>

21:24.290 --> 21:27.210
<b>Until the day I see Mr. Ryoma again...</b>

21:29.130 --> 21:31.760
